WEBVTT

00:00:09.070 --> 00:00:10.420
I'm a huge fan!

00:00:10.420 --> 00:00:11.260
We're all cheering for you!

00:00:11.580 --> 00:00:13.670
Th-Thank you very much!

00:00:13.950 --> 00:00:16.010
Th-Thank you.

00:00:16.380 --> 00:00:20.010
Thanks for supporting Candy Island!

00:01:51.270 --> 00:01:53.400
I heard you're gonna be on TV!

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:54.520
...Yeah...

00:01:54.910 --> 00:01:56.000
You're so lucky!

00:01:56.000 --> 00:01:57.840
What show is it?

00:01:57.840 --> 00:02:00.860
"Brain It Up! Brains Castle!!"

00:02:02.170 --> 00:02:05.690
The quiz game show
hosted by Mizuki and Airi?

00:02:05.690 --> 00:02:09.160
The one where idols
duke it out for PR timeow?

00:02:09.160 --> 00:02:11.670
It's like a battle of the idols... so cool!

00:02:12.600 --> 00:02:14.170
When's the shoot?

00:02:14.170 --> 00:02:14.920
Tomorrow.

00:02:15.930 --> 00:02:18.050
There's going to be
...a live studio audience too...

00:02:20.080 --> 00:02:22.540
It's our first time on TV.

00:02:22.540 --> 00:02:23.680
I'm really worried.

00:02:23.940 --> 00:02:26.780
Yeah, I'm worried too.

00:02:26.780 --> 00:02:31.950
We already released a single.
I figured we wouldn't have to work for a while.

00:02:31.950 --> 00:02:33.840
I'm gonna die from overwork.

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:34.730
Yeah, right!

00:02:36.630 --> 00:02:40.420
Remark, retort, and reaction!
The three R's of variety shows!

00:02:40.420 --> 00:02:43.570
Master these, and your worries will wane!

00:02:44.950 --> 00:02:46.830
Stand up! It's training time!

00:02:48.120 --> 00:02:49.660
Yeah, right!

00:02:49.660 --> 00:02:51.080
Yeah, right!

00:02:51.080 --> 00:02:52.750
Yeah, right!

00:02:52.750 --> 00:02:53.710
Yeah, right!

00:02:54.260 --> 00:02:55.460
Sharper! Like you're slapping them!

00:02:54.420 --> 00:02:55.460
Yeah, right!

00:02:55.890 --> 00:02:56.920
Yeah, right!

00:02:56.920 --> 00:02:58.550
With a snapping meowvement!

00:02:57.450 --> 00:02:58.550
Yeah, right!

00:02:59.060 --> 00:03:00.220
Yeah, right!

00:03:00.220 --> 00:03:01.870
Mew call that snap?

00:03:00.660 --> 00:03:01.870
Yeah, right!

00:03:01.870 --> 00:03:03.300
Anzu, you need to practice too.

00:03:02.250 --> 00:03:03.300
Yeah, right!

00:03:03.870 --> 00:03:05.700
I'll do the remarking.

00:03:04.060 --> 00:03:05.700
Yeah, right!

00:03:05.700 --> 00:03:07.110
Yeah, right!

00:03:07.110 --> 00:03:08.660
Yeah, right!

00:03:07.420 --> 00:03:09.380
Give a remark on this, then.

00:03:08.660 --> 00:03:10.060
Yeah, right!

00:03:10.500 --> 00:03:12.350
Spontaneity is the lifeblood of variety!

00:03:12.350 --> 00:03:13.400
Hop to it!

00:03:14.930 --> 00:03:16.900
I'll be the beetle.

00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:20.240
You just went to sleep!

00:03:21.270 --> 00:03:22.590
Nice retort.

00:03:22.590 --> 00:03:23.740
Good job, Miku-meow!

00:03:23.740 --> 00:03:25.750
It just came to meow.

00:03:25.750 --> 00:03:30.270
Listen up. Even the lamest remark
can be spiced by a good retort.

00:03:30.270 --> 00:03:30.870
You got that?

00:03:31.230 --> 00:03:31.870
Yes, ma'am!

00:03:33.260 --> 00:03:36.880
Make sure mew show the audience
that same spirit tomeowrrow!

00:03:38.100 --> 00:03:40.510
...I forgot all about the audience...

00:03:41.660 --> 00:03:44.490
That might be the first hurdle to clear.

00:03:49.890 --> 00:03:50.390
Come in.

00:03:51.570 --> 00:03:53.520
Hey, you got a minute?

00:03:56.210 --> 00:03:59.400
Do you like being an idol, Chieri?

00:03:59.910 --> 00:04:01.130
...Yeah...

00:04:01.130 --> 00:04:04.320
I like the cute dresses we get to wear.

00:04:04.880 --> 00:04:10.350
But it's so nerve-racking
to be in front of an audience.

00:04:10.350 --> 00:04:12.740
Yeah, it really <i>is</i>.

00:04:13.380 --> 00:04:16.420
I haven't gotten used to it either.

00:04:16.870 --> 00:04:19.790
I'd have so much fun if it were meow!

00:04:19.790 --> 00:04:22.040
And meow audience would too!

00:04:22.040 --> 00:04:22.820
You bet.

00:04:22.820 --> 00:04:24.670
Um... Excuse me.

00:04:28.710 --> 00:04:29.850
A frog?

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:33.430
Yeah, rich, right? It's totally wrong!

00:04:34.360 --> 00:04:35.940
What's going on meow?

00:04:35.940 --> 00:04:40.360
They say imagining the audience as
pumpkins helps with stage fright, right?

00:04:40.360 --> 00:04:42.050
But that's not a pumpkin.

00:04:43.030 --> 00:04:46.100
My apologies. This was all we had.

00:04:46.100 --> 00:04:49.950
I had hoped I could assist in some way.

00:04:52.460 --> 00:04:54.130
Thank you very much.

00:04:54.690 --> 00:04:56.540
I think I can do it now.

00:04:57.060 --> 00:04:59.290
Let's do our best for the show.

00:04:59.650 --> 00:05:00.620
We will!

00:05:00.620 --> 00:05:04.060
All right! Let's win and get that PR time!

00:05:04.060 --> 00:05:06.800
So everyone can hear our song!

00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:10.140
Let's go, Candy Island!

00:05:10.140 --> 00:05:11.560
Yeah!

00:05:14.460 --> 00:05:15.560
Yeah.

00:05:19.060 --> 00:05:23.510
Ieyasu, Hidetada, Iemitsu, Ietsuna, Tsunayoshi,

00:05:21.190 --> 00:05:24.060
...Frogs, frogs, frogs...

00:05:23.510 --> 00:05:28.820
...Ienobu, Ietsugu, Ie... Ie... Ie...

00:05:24.060 --> 00:05:24.940
Yeah, right.

00:05:24.940 --> 00:05:28.820
...Frogs, frogs, frogs...

00:05:26.160 --> 00:05:28.820
There's no point in worrying now.

00:05:29.140 --> 00:05:30.000
Yeah.

00:05:30.550 --> 00:05:33.790
Mio said they'd be coming too,
so let's do our best!

00:05:33.790 --> 00:05:35.050
O-Okay!

00:05:37.330 --> 00:05:39.670
Good morning!

00:05:39.670 --> 00:05:42.340
My last job went way over time.

00:05:42.970 --> 00:05:46.550
I guess I'm just too cute for my own good.

00:05:46.550 --> 00:05:47.220
Huh?

00:05:48.770 --> 00:05:50.850
Koshimizu Sachiko?

00:05:52.420 --> 00:05:53.400
Huh?

00:05:53.400 --> 00:05:54.720
Sachiko.

00:05:55.250 --> 00:05:57.250
I thought I heard ye.

00:05:57.250 --> 00:05:59.060
What brings thee to this room?

00:05:59.060 --> 00:06:01.230
Teasing the other contestants?

00:06:01.560 --> 00:06:03.230
...U-Um...

00:06:03.230 --> 00:06:06.740
Kobayakawa Sae and Himekawa Yuki!

00:06:06.740 --> 00:06:10.780
Perhaps thou hast the wrong dressing room?

00:06:10.780 --> 00:06:14.150
N-No way!

00:06:14.150 --> 00:06:19.050
...I was just...
giving these new idols some advice!

00:06:19.050 --> 00:06:20.370
Thou speakest truth?

00:06:21.470 --> 00:06:24.500
I hope a good fair match we shall have.

00:06:24.500 --> 00:06:27.130
Yes! We look forward to working with you!

00:06:27.500 --> 00:06:30.250
May no bodily harm befall us.

00:06:30.250 --> 00:06:31.940
I hope you warmed yourselves up!

00:06:31.940 --> 00:06:34.390
It's a rough show, but let's do our best!

00:06:35.020 --> 00:06:36.720
R-Right.

00:06:36.720 --> 00:06:37.610
Bodily harm?

00:06:37.610 --> 00:06:38.650
Rough?

00:06:38.650 --> 00:06:40.390
Isn't this a quiz show?

00:06:41.070 --> 00:06:42.820
They didn't tell you?

00:06:42.820 --> 00:06:46.900
Starting this week,
it's a physical action variety show.

00:06:50.020 --> 00:06:51.990
...They even changed the title...

00:06:56.970 --> 00:06:58.400
Hey, everybody!

00:06:58.400 --> 00:07:00.370
Feeling lame?

00:07:00.370 --> 00:07:01.870
Sure do!

00:07:02.290 --> 00:07:03.900
I know what you mean.

00:07:03.900 --> 00:07:07.200
Let's tame that lame with a game!

00:07:07.200 --> 00:07:11.410
Mizuki and Airi'll claim
your heart and light it aflame!

00:07:14.990 --> 00:07:17.370
Well then, let's get the night started!

00:07:17.930 --> 00:07:20.640
Brawn It Up! Muscle Castle!!

00:07:26.270 --> 00:07:27.460
All right.

00:07:27.460 --> 00:07:32.330
So, "Brain" turned into "Brawn", and the set's different too.

00:07:32.330 --> 00:07:34.980
Airi, did you hear why?

00:07:34.980 --> 00:07:41.010
Like, idols didn't have enough brains,
...so they couldn't call it—

00:07:39.590 --> 00:07:44.500
Well then, let's introduce the idols
competing for PR time tonight!

00:07:47.570 --> 00:07:51.050
In this corner, the usual suspects
who need no introduction!

00:07:51.050 --> 00:07:52.050
Yay!

00:07:52.050 --> 00:07:52.880
Let's do this!

00:07:53.340 --> 00:07:54.950
Welcome back!

00:07:54.950 --> 00:07:56.890
Now let's have your team name.

00:07:57.270 --> 00:07:58.680
..."KuteMe...

00:07:58.680 --> 00:07:59.450
...Baseball...

00:07:59.450 --> 00:08:01.890
...Ye Doth" doth call....

00:08:02.610 --> 00:08:07.300
And in this corner,
hitgirls sent by the Cinderella Project,

00:08:07.300 --> 00:08:10.920
three fresh faces
on their first TV appearance!

00:08:12.820 --> 00:08:14.540
Welcome!

00:08:14.540 --> 00:08:16.610
So what's your team's name?

00:08:17.430 --> 00:08:18.600
Okay.

00:08:18.600 --> 00:08:20.100
...One, two...

00:08:20.100 --> 00:08:21.970
Candy Island!

00:08:20.100 --> 00:08:22.870
C-Candy Island!

00:08:23.880 --> 00:08:26.020
They're so fresh!

00:08:27.090 --> 00:08:32.060
The KuteMe Baseball Ye Doth team
is already losing in freshness!

00:08:32.060 --> 00:08:33.880
Think you can win?

00:08:33.880 --> 00:08:35.500
Of course!

00:08:35.500 --> 00:08:38.120
After all, this cute me is on the team!

00:08:38.120 --> 00:08:39.740
Hold it!

00:08:39.740 --> 00:08:43.020
No trash talk without the mic!

00:08:45.300 --> 00:08:48.690
You! What was it... Candy Island?

00:08:49.030 --> 00:08:51.520
If you think we'll be
sweet and easy on you,

00:08:51.520 --> 00:08:54.570
you're in for a licking
from cute me and this show!

00:08:55.690 --> 00:08:56.950
I'm so sorry!

00:08:57.600 --> 00:08:59.940
Oh, she apologized!

00:08:59.940 --> 00:09:01.230
10 points!

00:09:01.230 --> 00:09:02.200
Huh?

00:09:04.780 --> 00:09:07.960
The Candy team wins the first round!

00:09:09.500 --> 00:09:10.960
And cut!

00:09:11.630 --> 00:09:14.940
I feel like a mother watching her children.

00:09:14.940 --> 00:09:18.580
...The audience liked it...
but Chieri's just panicking, right?

00:09:18.580 --> 00:09:21.830
Well, they got points for it,
so they're off to a good start.

00:09:21.830 --> 00:09:22.600
No!

00:09:22.870 --> 00:09:26.850
That was a brilliant move by the host
to keep the show spontaneous.

00:09:27.520 --> 00:09:29.730
The real battle starts now.

00:09:30.690 --> 00:09:32.410
...I'm so nervous...

00:09:32.410 --> 00:09:34.260
Are you okay, Chieri?

00:09:34.260 --> 00:09:35.460
Y-Yes.

00:09:35.460 --> 00:09:37.100
...No...

00:09:37.100 --> 00:09:41.460
Sorry, my mind goes blank
whenever I hear the audience.

00:09:43.360 --> 00:09:46.000
Hey, remember that? They're frogs.

00:09:47.260 --> 00:09:49.180
Right! They're frogs!

00:09:49.180 --> 00:09:50.380
Just relax.

00:09:51.160 --> 00:09:52.700
...Okay...

00:09:52.700 --> 00:09:54.880
...Frogs, frogs...

00:09:55.330 --> 00:09:58.130
Burst Their Bubble!

00:09:58.380 --> 00:09:59.890
The rules are simple!

00:09:59.890 --> 00:10:02.890
Whichever team pops the
other team's balloon first wins!

00:10:03.240 --> 00:10:06.640
Who will be the true brawn idol?

00:10:16.610 --> 00:10:18.560
Look at those balloons inflate!

00:10:18.560 --> 00:10:20.990
Looks like the Baseball Ye Doth team
has the advantage.

00:10:24.930 --> 00:10:26.870
No, stay away!

00:10:30.380 --> 00:10:32.000
...Oh, my heart...

00:10:32.000 --> 00:10:35.000
Winner: the Baseball Ye Doth team!

00:10:32.740 --> 00:10:35.000
Totally sweet, Mimucchi!

00:10:37.690 --> 00:10:40.460
Baseball Ye Doth has taken the lead!

00:10:40.460 --> 00:10:44.660
Kawashima, what about KuteMe?

00:10:44.660 --> 00:10:47.390
And that means the losers
will get the "star treatment"!

00:10:48.470 --> 00:10:52.730
Candy will be drinking this "health drink".

00:10:52.990 --> 00:10:54.480
Um... What does it taste like?

00:10:55.310 --> 00:10:56.980
Just chug it!

00:11:00.570 --> 00:11:03.320
I-It's so bitter!

00:11:03.630 --> 00:11:05.950
Come on, Anzu! Drink it all up!

00:11:05.950 --> 00:11:07.370
No way, no way, no way!

00:11:07.370 --> 00:11:09.250
Hang in there!

00:11:07.370 --> 00:11:09.250
Nice reaction!

00:11:11.040 --> 00:11:13.170
Marshmallow Catching!

00:11:14.600 --> 00:11:16.420
Who wants to catch?

00:11:16.420 --> 00:11:17.350
Me!

00:11:17.350 --> 00:11:19.170
Ooh, we've got eager beavers!

00:11:19.700 --> 00:11:21.260
Catching's my bag!

00:11:21.580 --> 00:11:23.990
I wanna eat those marshmallows!

00:11:23.990 --> 00:11:25.670
My, you're honest.

00:11:26.840 --> 00:11:29.010
Who wants to shoot the marshmallow gun?

00:11:29.010 --> 00:11:29.970
Me!

00:11:30.740 --> 00:11:32.490
There we have it!

00:11:31.320 --> 00:11:33.230
It's all yours.

00:11:33.620 --> 00:11:38.060
Sae and Anzu will be
participating in the next competition,

00:11:38.060 --> 00:11:39.110
so they'll be going backstage to prepare!

00:11:39.520 --> 00:11:40.110
Huh?

00:11:40.360 --> 00:11:42.740
First up, Ye Doth!

00:11:42.740 --> 00:11:43.990
Bring it on!

00:11:44.280 --> 00:11:46.210
You got it!

00:11:46.210 --> 00:11:47.870
Leave it to me!

00:11:48.220 --> 00:11:51.040
I'll shoot it right in your mouth!

00:11:54.360 --> 00:11:55.750
Oops. Sorry.

00:11:56.000 --> 00:11:57.110
...Sachiko...

00:11:57.110 --> 00:11:59.500
Sachiko, that was too close!
No points for you.

00:11:59.500 --> 00:12:00.930
What?!

00:12:00.930 --> 00:12:03.010
Candy's up next!

00:12:03.010 --> 00:12:04.630
Go for it!

00:12:03.010 --> 00:12:04.630
You can do it!

00:12:05.620 --> 00:12:06.840
...Frogs...

00:12:12.530 --> 00:12:13.940
...The marshmallow...

00:12:13.940 --> 00:12:15.680
A beautiful dive!

00:12:15.680 --> 00:12:18.190
You can tell she really wanted it.

00:12:21.650 --> 00:12:23.030
Got it!

00:12:27.450 --> 00:12:28.910
...And...

00:12:29.760 --> 00:12:31.080
We did it!

00:12:30.540 --> 00:12:34.130
My circuits were shorted a long time ago

00:12:34.130 --> 00:12:37.220
Maybe I've become a human being

00:12:34.580 --> 00:12:36.850
Now it's Candy with the last shot!

00:12:36.780 --> 00:12:37.740
oh wow!

00:12:36.850 --> 00:12:38.890
If they catch this, it'll be a tie.

00:12:37.220 --> 00:12:41.070
Is this what they mean by a miracle?

00:12:38.890 --> 00:12:40.590
You can do it, Kanako!

00:12:40.380 --> 00:12:42.150
chraat chraat

00:12:40.850 --> 00:12:42.540
Yeah.

00:12:41.790 --> 00:12:45.480
Starting today, I'm falling in love

00:12:42.540 --> 00:12:44.220
Ready, Chieri?

00:12:44.490 --> 00:12:45.460
Yeah.

00:12:45.480 --> 00:12:47.680
I'm a girl, you know

00:12:47.400 --> 00:12:48.840
ta-da

00:12:55.020 --> 00:12:56.640
I caught it!

00:12:57.030 --> 00:12:58.060
...Thank goodness...

00:12:58.850 --> 00:13:00.940
Kanako, what do you think?

00:13:02.710 --> 00:13:03.820
It's yummy!

00:13:05.320 --> 00:13:09.100
Since no one lost, no one gets the star treatment.

00:13:05.610 --> 00:13:07.370
Good job, Kanako!

00:13:07.370 --> 00:13:08.360
Yeah.

00:13:08.360 --> 00:13:11.950
It was like the god of sweets
granted her a miracle.

00:13:09.100 --> 00:13:11.950
We'll be back after a word from our sponsors!

00:13:12.380 --> 00:13:14.200
They might be in the running!

00:13:16.300 --> 00:13:23.420
Fashion: a muscle that all girls
must train daily to perfection.

00:13:23.420 --> 00:13:27.340
So next up we'll have
a plain clothes fashion show!

00:13:29.090 --> 00:13:33.850
First up, a fairy from remote
Hokkaido: Futaba Anzu.

00:13:35.350 --> 00:13:41.480
Sporting a casual shirt and shorts,
and carrying her bunny in one hand.

00:13:41.820 --> 00:13:44.880
The phrase, "You Work, You Lose"
is written on her shirt.

00:13:44.880 --> 00:13:48.430
Cue a new era in idol style.

00:13:48.430 --> 00:13:50.740
Wait, this might be a little <i>too</i> new.

00:13:52.840 --> 00:13:53.990
They like it.

00:13:54.560 --> 00:13:56.000
...And next up, we have...

00:13:58.350 --> 00:14:02.750
A nymph from the land of Kyoto:
Kobayakawa Sae.

00:14:03.450 --> 00:14:05.760
She isn't wearing one of her
usual kimonos today.

00:14:05.760 --> 00:14:08.330
It's a school uniform.
What a difference it makes!

00:14:08.830 --> 00:14:11.510
...For I came from school, today, directly...

00:14:13.010 --> 00:14:14.940
...Hngh...

00:14:14.940 --> 00:14:16.580
60 points!

00:14:16.580 --> 00:14:17.890
All right!

00:14:16.940 --> 00:14:17.890
Awesome!

00:14:19.390 --> 00:14:24.020
And Candy gets the star treatment! Health drink!

00:14:20.320 --> 00:14:24.020
Good job, Anzu. You left a mark.

00:14:26.590 --> 00:14:28.860
And now we've come to the final event.

00:14:29.230 --> 00:14:32.110
If you win, it's big money!
A comeback can be yours!

00:14:32.350 --> 00:14:34.950
And the winner gets that PR time!

00:14:35.260 --> 00:14:40.510
The loser, however,
gets the real star treatment!

00:14:40.510 --> 00:14:43.500
A bungee jumping experience
into this beautiful scenery!

00:14:43.770 --> 00:14:45.130
...W-Wait...

00:14:46.010 --> 00:14:46.880
...N-No way...

00:14:48.260 --> 00:14:50.510
That's going a bit overboard, staff-o.

00:14:50.510 --> 00:14:52.000
And cut!

00:14:53.150 --> 00:14:54.460
What do we do?

00:14:54.460 --> 00:14:58.260
Producer, I don't think we can do this.

00:14:58.260 --> 00:14:59.880
It's part of the job.

00:14:59.880 --> 00:15:00.430
...And—

00:15:02.560 --> 00:15:03.810
Chieri?!

00:15:03.810 --> 00:15:04.670
Ogata!

00:15:10.520 --> 00:15:11.570
Are you all right?

00:15:12.130 --> 00:15:13.320
Yes.

00:15:13.320 --> 00:15:14.820
I'm so sorry.

00:15:17.700 --> 00:15:20.530
Can you do the next segment?

00:15:22.270 --> 00:15:23.260
Yes.

00:15:23.940 --> 00:15:25.840
Can you do it with a smile?

00:15:31.710 --> 00:15:32.470
Chieri,

00:15:33.010 --> 00:15:35.860
I'm scared of bungee jumping too,

00:15:35.860 --> 00:15:39.080
but I'll try to smile
through the whole segment.

00:15:39.080 --> 00:15:39.720
...So...

00:15:42.310 --> 00:15:47.650
I'm really glad that I could
debut with you in this unit.

00:15:48.710 --> 00:15:51.860
I'd never have been able
to make it this far by myself.

00:15:53.700 --> 00:15:54.880
I'm scared,

00:15:55.590 --> 00:15:58.830
and I don't know if I'll be able
to smile through the whole thing,

00:15:59.120 --> 00:16:03.540
but you've given me courage.

00:16:05.570 --> 00:16:06.830
I want to do it.

00:16:08.460 --> 00:16:09.300
Yeah!

00:16:09.300 --> 00:16:10.700
Let's do it together!

00:16:10.700 --> 00:16:13.740
If we're together,
even bungee jumping won't be scary!

00:16:13.740 --> 00:16:15.380
No, it'll still be scary.

00:16:15.380 --> 00:16:17.090
...Yeah, you're right...

00:16:18.650 --> 00:16:22.850
I don't wanna go bungee jumping,
so I say we make a comeback.

00:16:23.910 --> 00:16:26.840
That's right!
We can just make a comeback!

00:16:26.840 --> 00:16:29.110
We'll get the PR time too!

00:16:29.540 --> 00:16:31.610
Let's share our song with everyone!

00:16:32.070 --> 00:16:32.780
Yeah!

00:16:34.280 --> 00:16:37.100
Let's go, Candy Island!

00:16:37.100 --> 00:16:38.280
Yeah!

00:16:42.180 --> 00:16:44.180
And we're back!

00:16:44.180 --> 00:16:46.100
Let's give it up for our last game!

00:16:46.100 --> 00:16:48.790
...Put brains and brawn together, and you get...

00:16:48.790 --> 00:16:50.670
Slideopardy!

00:16:52.690 --> 00:16:56.090
The team with any remaining
members wins the game.

00:16:56.090 --> 00:16:58.550
The losing team gets no points.

00:16:59.180 --> 00:17:01.560
Choose questions
from the panels on the board.

00:17:02.030 --> 00:17:03.860
First to answer gets command of the board.

00:17:03.860 --> 00:17:07.940
Each correct answer raises
one end of the opponents' slide.

00:17:08.250 --> 00:17:09.750
Now for our first question.

00:17:09.750 --> 00:17:11.570
We'll start with Showbiz for 10.

00:17:13.340 --> 00:17:19.570
This team gave an answer so ditzy that the show
had to change its format to accommodate.

00:17:19.570 --> 00:17:21.460
Who is Team BB?

00:17:21.460 --> 00:17:22.910
Point to Sachiko!

00:17:22.910 --> 00:17:25.330
You almost had it, Kanako.

00:17:28.380 --> 00:17:30.180
Don't fall just yet!

00:17:30.180 --> 00:17:32.840
Ye Doth, what question will we have next?

00:17:32.840 --> 00:17:34.460
Showbiz for 20!

00:17:35.970 --> 00:17:41.600
This three-man unit has been on
their national tour since this past April.

00:17:42.910 --> 00:17:43.900
Who is Jupiter?

00:17:43.900 --> 00:17:45.020
That's right!

00:17:47.650 --> 00:17:48.980
What is Rio de Janeiro?

00:17:48.980 --> 00:17:50.020
That's right!

00:17:50.020 --> 00:17:51.020
All right!

00:17:53.660 --> 00:17:55.040
I'm done for.

00:17:55.040 --> 00:17:55.650
No!

00:17:56.210 --> 00:17:57.800
Let's do this together!

00:17:57.800 --> 00:17:59.160
Yeah.

00:18:00.770 --> 00:18:02.770
We'll finish you with this next one.

00:18:02.770 --> 00:18:04.250
History for 10!

00:18:05.880 --> 00:18:08.980
This man was the third shogun
of the Tokugawa Shogunate.

00:18:09.710 --> 00:18:10.330
Huh?

00:18:10.330 --> 00:18:11.250
...U-Um...

00:18:11.600 --> 00:18:12.630
Who is Iemitsu?

00:18:14.230 --> 00:18:15.710
That's right, Kanako!

00:18:15.710 --> 00:18:16.550
You did it!

00:18:16.550 --> 00:18:18.110
Good job, Kanako!

00:18:22.040 --> 00:18:25.220
This might be your ticket to safety, Candy!

00:18:25.460 --> 00:18:27.350
Science for 30.

00:18:27.350 --> 00:18:30.190
Swinging big there, Candy!

00:18:30.420 --> 00:18:32.040
A-Anzu?

00:18:32.040 --> 00:18:34.440
This is the only way for us to win.

00:18:36.110 --> 00:18:39.140
Suppose you dropped an apple
from the top of the Tokyo Skytree.

00:18:39.140 --> 00:18:42.200
What will be the velocity of the apple
at the instant before it hits the ground?

00:18:42.580 --> 00:18:45.570
The height of the
Tokyo Skytree is 634 meters.

00:18:45.570 --> 00:18:47.950
Assume that gravitational acceleration is
a constant is 9.8 meters per second squared.

00:18:49.520 --> 00:18:52.420
111.474 meters per second.

00:18:53.880 --> 00:18:55.170
...Um...

00:18:55.170 --> 00:18:56.170
And in kilometers per hour?

00:18:56.170 --> 00:18:58.590
401.306 km!

00:18:59.470 --> 00:19:01.090
That's right!

00:19:01.460 --> 00:19:03.220
Did you do all that in your head?!

00:19:03.220 --> 00:19:04.980
...Thou art amazing...

00:19:08.390 --> 00:19:11.540
Oh, do we have our first fall?

00:19:11.540 --> 00:19:13.850
She's holding on in a weird position!

00:19:14.800 --> 00:19:16.480
What's the next question?

00:19:16.780 --> 00:19:17.980
Cartoons for 30.

00:19:17.980 --> 00:19:20.990
Oh, another 30-pointer?

00:19:22.950 --> 00:19:27.400
Where was the heroine of Out-of-Body Experience:
Beedakrappoutuvya, Beedakrappoutuvya, born?

00:19:27.400 --> 00:19:29.980
Apartment 6 of Number 6, Sixth Street, Pluto!

00:19:29.980 --> 00:19:31.880
That's right!

00:19:32.590 --> 00:19:34.910
Is there anything she can't field?

00:19:37.340 --> 00:19:38.550
I... can't hold on any longer.

00:19:40.760 --> 00:19:43.010
And Sae's down!

00:19:43.400 --> 00:19:45.420
I beg for your forgiveness.

00:19:45.420 --> 00:19:47.510
Next question! Hurry!

00:19:47.800 --> 00:19:49.720
Grab Bag for 30!

00:19:49.720 --> 00:19:52.210
A 30-pointer in the random category!

00:19:50.690 --> 00:19:51.700
You can do it!

00:19:51.700 --> 00:19:53.790
She's going for the win.

00:19:52.210 --> 00:19:54.350
Can nothing stop her?

00:19:55.900 --> 00:19:57.910
During the Edo period,

00:19:57.910 --> 00:20:01.620
Dutch traders introduced this non-native species to Japan
when they used it as packaging material for glass wares.

00:20:01.620 --> 00:20:05.030
What is the name of this flower, which
symbolizes "good fortune" and "promises"?

00:20:06.720 --> 00:20:08.240
Sorry, I don't know.

00:20:08.240 --> 00:20:09.990
What?!

00:20:11.720 --> 00:20:12.880
...Um...

00:20:12.880 --> 00:20:16.050
If no one knows the answer,
Ye Doth gets command of the board.

00:20:16.050 --> 00:20:16.970
Here!

00:20:18.510 --> 00:20:20.260
Do you know, Chieri?

00:20:22.260 --> 00:20:23.970
...The answer is...

00:20:24.940 --> 00:20:26.340
white clover!

00:20:28.920 --> 00:20:30.600
That's right!

00:20:31.180 --> 00:20:33.180
Wow, Chieri!

00:20:33.180 --> 00:20:33.850
You did it!

00:20:34.910 --> 00:20:36.100
Yeah!

00:20:36.100 --> 00:20:40.970
Candy has just gotten three
30-pointers right in a row!

00:20:36.580 --> 00:20:38.360
...White clover...

00:20:38.360 --> 00:20:40.310
Yeah, like four-leaf clover.

00:20:40.310 --> 00:20:42.610
They really do bring good luck!

00:20:40.970 --> 00:20:42.610
Unbelievable!

00:20:43.120 --> 00:20:46.070
Okay, Ye Doth! Up you go!

00:20:46.070 --> 00:20:49.420
...I'm falling...

00:20:53.800 --> 00:20:57.460
That was a cute fall there, Sachiko.

00:20:57.460 --> 00:21:00.840
And that makes Candy the winner!

00:21:04.430 --> 00:21:05.220
...We won...

00:21:06.740 --> 00:21:07.720
Yeah.

00:21:07.720 --> 00:21:09.010
Anzu!

00:21:09.010 --> 00:21:12.220
We won!

00:21:15.500 --> 00:21:16.690
And cut!

00:21:19.420 --> 00:21:22.690
Man, going serious is exhausting.

00:21:27.460 --> 00:21:29.200
Oh, Mio's here.

00:21:30.010 --> 00:21:31.950
Rin and Uzuki too.

00:21:32.590 --> 00:21:34.420
You <i>just</i> noticed?

00:21:34.420 --> 00:21:36.020
They've been here since the start.

00:21:36.020 --> 00:21:39.930
Sorry. They were frogs until a second ago.

00:21:41.230 --> 00:21:42.960
Well, whatever.

00:21:43.860 --> 00:21:45.460
And now for the results!

00:21:48.820 --> 00:21:50.470
Oh wow, it's a tie.

00:21:51.120 --> 00:21:53.350
You're like good friends already.

00:21:53.350 --> 00:21:56.770
So you'll share the
PR time evenly like friends.

00:21:56.770 --> 00:21:59.700
And get the star treatment
together like friends too.

00:21:59.700 --> 00:22:00.940
What?!

00:22:00.940 --> 00:22:02.900
We didn't hear about this!

00:22:02.900 --> 00:22:05.550
They said not to tell you.

00:22:05.550 --> 00:22:07.100
No way!

00:22:06.240 --> 00:22:11.740
So next week's show will be a
Candy-Ye Doth bungee jumping special!

00:22:11.740 --> 00:22:16.730
We have a lot of other stuff planned,
so be sure to tune in!

00:22:13.540 --> 00:22:16.250
We got another job.

00:22:16.730 --> 00:22:19.500
But don't go away! We still have
our idols' PR time!

00:22:18.110 --> 00:22:19.500
...No way...

00:22:20.010 --> 00:22:23.000
This wasn't supposed to happen!

00:22:30.130 --> 00:22:32.630
Hi there, everyone!

00:22:32.630 --> 00:22:34.020
...One, two...

00:22:34.020 --> 00:22:36.020
We're Candy Island!

00:22:36.350 --> 00:22:42.180
The song playing now is
our recently released debut single,

00:22:42.180 --> 00:22:44.150
Happy×2 Days.

00:22:44.560 --> 00:22:47.810
As for why it's "Happy×2",

00:22:47.810 --> 00:22:51.380
it's because the more happy, the better.

00:22:51.380 --> 00:22:54.280
We hope our song
can make everyone happy too.

00:22:54.640 --> 00:22:56.790
It's a great song!
We hope you'll give it a listen!

00:22:57.060 --> 00:22:58.530
Please give it a listen!

00:22:58.530 --> 00:23:01.550
And also, we'll be retiring!

00:23:03.130 --> 00:23:04.530
Yeah, right!
